From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 05:17:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] HID: apple-mtp-haptic: check the click strength again on
 resume

The strength from apple,click-strength is written into the actuator
firmware at probe only. Check it again on resume and reset_resume, and
write it back if the firmware no longer has it, the same way as at probe.

On the MTP machines the coprocessor keeps running across suspend-to-idle
and nothing is known to clear the waveforms, so this is expected to find
the strength in place and write nothing. That has not been confirmed on
hardware, and the check costs two feature report reads. A debug message
now says when a strength is written, so a resume that had to restore it
shows up with dynamic debug.

The MTP firmware is not restarted while Linux runs. rtkit-helper has no
crash recovery, it and dockchannel-hid both refuse sysfs unbind, and the
coprocessor announces its interfaces once per boot. The actuator can only
come back as a new HID device, and probe already sets the strength there.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
(cherry picked from commit bd1fabcf757027dc53e154fc881d56d245c65bdf)
---
 drivers/hid/hid-apple-mtp-haptic.c | 15 ++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/hid/hid-apple-mtp-haptic.c b/drivers/hid/hid-apple-mtp-haptic.c
index 2a8f452b96..578afd24ef 100644
--- a/drivers/hid/hid-apple-mtp-haptic.c
+++ b/drivers/hid/hid-apple-mtp-haptic.c
@@ -86,6 +86,9 @@ EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(apple_taptic_switch_modes);
  * fainter than the same pad gives under macOS. A machine whose device tree
  * gives the actuator a click strength has it written over the firmware's,
  * leaving the shape of each waveform as the firmware has it.
+ *
+ * The strength is firmware state, so it is checked again on every resume
+ * the transport passes on, and written if the firmware no longer has it.
  */
 #define APPLE_TAPTIC_PRESS_WAVEFORM	0x22
 #define APPLE_TAPTIC_RELEASE_WAVEFORM	0x23
@@ -111,6 +114,8 @@ static int apple_taptic_set_strength(struct hid_device *haptic_hdev, u8 report,
 	if (buf[APPLE_TAPTIC_WAVEFORM_STRENGTH] == strength)
 		return 0;
 
+	hid_dbg(haptic_hdev, "click waveform 0x%02x strength 0x%02x -> 0x%02x\n",
+		report, buf[APPLE_TAPTIC_WAVEFORM_STRENGTH], strength);
 	buf[APPLE_TAPTIC_WAVEFORM_STRENGTH] = strength;
 	len = hid_hw_raw_request(haptic_hdev, report, buf, len,
 				 HID_FEATURE_REPORT, HID_REQ_SET_REPORT);
@@ -194,6 +199,12 @@ static int apple_actuator_probe(struct hid_device *haptic_hdev, const struct hid
 	return 0;
 }
 
+static int apple_actuator_resume(struct hid_device *haptic_hdev)
+{
+	apple_taptic_set_click_strength(haptic_hdev);
+	return 0;
+}
+
 static bool actuator_match(struct hid_device *hdev, bool ignore_special_drivers)
 {
 	return apple_taptic_is_actuator(hdev);
@@ -219,7 +230,9 @@ static struct hid_driver apple_actuator_driver = {
 	.id_table = apple_haptic_devices,
 	.probe = apple_actuator_probe,
 	.match = actuator_match,
-	.remove = actuator_remove
+	.remove = actuator_remove,
+	.resume = pm_ptr(apple_actuator_resume),
+	.reset_resume = pm_ptr(apple_actuator_resume),
 };
 module_hid_driver(apple_actuator_driver);
 
